---
/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   What happens after treatment.

   Closes a real gap: the site previously ended at discharge, and "then what?"
   is a question both patients and families ask when choosing a programme.

   Built on CASE MANAGEMENT, which is corroborated on 32 of 571 calls (5.6%) —
   above the working threshold — rather than on the wiki's twelve aftercare
   services, of which almost none is evidenced.

   Corroborating quotes:
     "before she leaves residential, she does have a case manager... they can
      get her all set up with getting a primary care provider, getting a
      psychiatrist, getting a therapist"
     "the case manager will help me find somewhere to go to afterwards"
     "detox should have a case manager or a social worker that talks with the
      client and asks them what they wanna do"
     "the case manager should be able to set her up with medical transport at
      discharge"
     "you work with a case manager to see what your aftercare program is gonna
      look like"

   ⚠ The URL keeps "alumni" to stay aligned with the sitemap row, but the page
   deliberately does NOT claim an alumni app, alumni events or reunions. Alumni
   appears in 2 calls and none of those services is corroborated. Retitle the
   sitemap row rather than adding them back.

   Note the psychiatry line is consistent with the sitewide correction: care is
   ARRANGED for outside, not prescribed here.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TopBar from '../../components/TopBar.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';

import AfterHero from '../../components/after/AfterHero.astro';
import YourCaseManager from '../../components/after/YourCaseManager.astro';
import AfterQuestions from '../../components/after/AfterQuestions.astro';

import Testimonials from '../../components/Testimonials.astro';
import VerifySection from '../../components/VerifySection.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../../components/FinalCTA.astro';

const title = 'What Happens After Treatment | Buena Vista Health & Recovery, Chandler AZ';
const description =
  'Discharge planning starts early in your stay: ongoing therapy, a primary care provider, somewhere to live and the journey home, arranged before you leave. Call (888) 362-5576.';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    ['When does discharge planning start at Buena Vista?',
     'Early in the stay rather than the final week. A case manager is assigned in detox and again in residential, and planning for what comes next begins while there is time to arrange it.'],
    ['What is arranged before I leave treatment?',
     'Ongoing therapy, psychiatric care where it applies, a primary care provider, housing if home is not viable, and transport home — so the week after discharge has appointments in it rather than a gap.'],
    ['Does Buena Vista provide outpatient treatment after residential?',
     'Not at present — an intensive outpatient programme is being built. Until it opens, case managers help people find an outpatient programme that accepts their insurance.'],
    ['What happens if I relapse after treatment?',
     'You can call again. Returning is a normal part of recovery for many people and there is no limit on how many times someone can try.'],
  ].map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <TopBar />
  <Nav />

  <AfterHero />
  <YourCaseManager />
  <Testimonials />
  <VerifySection />
  <AfterQuestions />

  <FinalCTA />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} is:inline />
</Layout>
